      "location_name": "Marwari - Joshimath Highway Mile 38",
      "latitude": 30.5564,
      "longitude": 79.5653,
      "photo_url": "/api/v1/media/rep_img_1788556424379_d455wo.jpg",
      "photo_storage_key": "rep_img_1788556424379_d455wo.jpg",
      "verification_status": "RESOLVED",
      "ai_observation": "AI ASSESSMENT — VERIFY BEFORE RESPONSE: Preliminary technical evaluation of the reported incident at NH-58 (Mile 38) indicates an active slope failure characterized by a steep scarp face with exposed soil and loose colluvium/rock debris. The reported crown tension cracks and slope toe failure suggest ongoing displacement driven by surface drainage accumulation and poor runoff control. The resulting hazard poses an immediate risk of road surface obstruction and shoulder subsidence along the national highway corridor. This assessment is strictly preliminary and requires urgent ground truth verification and structural appraisal by GSI/NDMA field teams.",
      "admin_notes": "BRO clearing team removed boulders, installed catch nets, and restored traffic flow.",
      "created_at": "2026-09-04T21:13:44.448Z",
      "updated_at": "2026-09-04T21:13:51.553Z"
    },
